# 0030-screensaver-font-fits-panel -- metadata and post-conditions.
#
# WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS
#
# Operator, from hardware, 2026-08-16: *"the screensaver in desktop mode appears
# clipped. as if it were meant for a bigger screen so then the O and Y of
# omarchy can't be seen."*
#
# The screensaver is `ttfx` rendering ~/.config/omarchy/branding/screensaver.txt
# inside a fullscreen terminal. The art is UPSTREAM'S OWN logo.txt, copied to
# that path by omarchy-upgrade-to-quattro:1972, and it is **81 columns wide**
# (measured: `max(len(line))` over the pinned checkout's logo.txt at
# basecamp/omarchy@f0020448ca87; the "O" occupies columns 0-9 and the "Y"
# columns 70-80 -- exactly the two letters the operator lost).
#
# THE TERMINAL IS foot, AND THAT IS MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED. Two independent
# readings agree:
#   * default/xdg-terminal-exec/hyprland-xdg-terminals.list names `foot.desktop`
#     and nothing else, and omarchy-launch-screensaver picks the terminal with
#     `xdg-terminal-exec --print-id`;
#   * `hyprctl -j clients` read off this Deck 2026-08-12 with the screensaver
#     actually playing reported {"class":"org.omarchy.screensaver",
#     "title":"foot","fullscreen":2} -- transcribed in
#     src/deck-input-mapper.py:1754.
# install/omarchy-base.packages:42 carries `foot`; alacritty, ghostty and kitty
# are not installed on the target at all.
#
# THE ARITHMETIC, and why 18 cannot work on this panel
#
# eDP-1 is 800x1280 physical, `transform: 3`, `scale: 1.25` (docs/PROGRESS.md
# §5.37 / line 3449), so a fullscreen window's LOGICAL width is 1024 px --
# not 1280. `o.window("org.omarchy.screensaver", { fullscreen = true })` in
# default/hypr/apps/system.lua is what makes it fullscreen.
#
# JetBrainsMono Nerd Font is 1000 units/em with a 600-unit advance on every
# glyph the art uses -- U+2588/U+2584/U+2580 and space all measure 600
# (read from JetBrainsMonoNerdFont-Regular.ttf with fontTools). A terminal cell
# is therefore 0.6 em wide, so:
#
#     columns ~= 1024 / (size_pt * 96/72 * 0.6) = 1280 / size_pt
#
# 🔴 THE SCALE FACTOR CANCELS, so this holds whether foot uses the fractional
# scale (1.25) or falls back to integer scaling (2): the buffer and the font
# grow by the same factor, and the column count depends only on the LOGICAL
# width. That is what makes this number safe to pin.
#
#     size=18 -> 71 columns   art needs 81 -> 10 columns lost, 5 per side
#     size=16 -> 80 columns   still one short
#     size=15 -> 85 columns   fits, 4 spare
#     size=14 -> 91 columns   fits, 10 spare        <- this patch
#
# 71 columns is also the reading that MATCHES THE SYMPTOM and no other does:
# 5 columns off each side takes exactly half the O and half the Y. Integer-2
# scaling without the cancellation would have cost 37 columns (four letters);
# no scaling at all would have given 91 and clipped nothing.
#
# ⚠️ THE `wait_for_terminal_resize` RACE IS NOT THE CAUSE, and was checked
# rather than assumed. omarchy-screensaver's own comment warns that ttfx
# measures the terminal once at startup and that an 80x24 pty paints into the
# corner. But an 80-column canvas would clip the 81-column art by ONE column,
# not by half of two letters, and the observed art is centred rather than
# cornered. The race would make the bug worse; it cannot produce it. Do not
# "fix" the font and the race together and then not know which one mattered.
#
# WHY 14 AND NOT 15. 15 fits with 4 columns to spare, which is inside the
# rounding noise: foot derives the cell width through fcft/FreeType at an
# integer pixel size, and one pixel either way moves the cell from 15 to 16 and
# the column count from 85 to 80 -- back under the art. 14 survives that (a
# 15 px cell still yields 85 columns) and also clears 80 columns, which is
# `omarchy-transcode-ascii`'s DEFAULT --width -- so custom branding produced
# the documented way keeps fitting too.
#
# ⚠️ SCOPE: foot only, deliberately. default/alacritty/screensaver.toml and
# omarchy-launch-screensaver's `--font-size=18` for ghostty and kitty carry the
# same 18 and would have the same bug, but none of those three terminals is on
# the target and patching a file nothing reads is drift surface for no measured
# benefit. If the Deck's terminal ever changes, this patch changes with it.
#
# ⚠️ NOT VERIFIED ON HARDWARE. The Deck was mid-install when this was written
# and sshd was gone; nobody has seen the result on a panel. What IS verified is
# that the patch applies to the pin, that the arithmetic above is measured from
# the real font file and the real art file, and that the terminal is foot.
#
# ⚠️ NOT AN LCD CLAIM. The numbers above come from the OLED's eDP-1 as read on
# this Deck. The LCD model is not tested and nothing here asserts it works
# (CLAUDE.md). A smaller screensaver font cannot break an untested panel worse
# than an oversized one, but that is a tolerance argument, not a test result.
#
# No qmllint post-condition: this is a foot INI, not QML. The applier requires
# at least one post-condition per patch, and the assert_counts below are it.

requirement: docs/tasks/P33-fix-round.md (screensaver clipping, operator 2026-08-16) / docs/PROGRESS.md §5.37
description: size the screensaver terminal font so Omarchy's 81-column logo fits the Deck's 1024-logical-px-wide panel
target: default/foot/screensaver.ini

# Exactly once, and exactly this value. Twice would mean a previous run appended
# rather than patched.
assert_count: default/foot/screensaver.ini|^font=JetBrainsMono Nerd Font:size=7$|1
# Nothing left at 16 or above. 1280/16 = 80 columns, one short of the 81-column
# art -- so any size in that range is the bug, whoever wrote it. Written as a
# range rather than as `size=18` so an upstream retune to 17, 20 or 24 is caught
# too: 0020's history is that upstream retunes literals and a patch pinned to
# one literal stops meaning anything.
assert_count: default/foot/screensaver.ini|^font=.*:size=(1[6-9]|[2-9][0-9]|[0-9]{3,})$|0
